WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:02.795
- [Narrator] In Switzerland,
on the coast of Lake Geneva,

00:00:02.795 --> 00:00:04.769
sits the quiet town of Montreux.

00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:06.673
- [Roger] It was a
place where people went

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.204
to retire to, lots of, lots of tea shops

00:00:09.204 --> 00:00:11.755
and little old ladies kind of place.

00:00:11.755 --> 00:00:14.611
- [Narrator] But on December 4, 1971,

00:00:14.611 --> 00:00:16.632
a giant fire at the local
concert hall took hold,

00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:19.163
eventually leading this man.

00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:20.997
- [Roger] My name is Roger
Glover, I'm the bass player

00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:22.251
of Deep Purple.

00:00:22.251 --> 00:00:23.725
- [Narrator] To help write this song.

00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:27.225
(rock instrumental music)

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.519
So let's rewind a bit.

00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:34.725
Deep Purple just arrived in Switzerland,

00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:37.024
planning to record their
next album, Machine Head

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:38.440
at a local concert venue.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.228
But they couldn't start until Frank Zappa

00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:41.061
and The Mothers of Invention finished

00:00:41.061 --> 00:00:43.688
their show that afternoon.

00:00:43.688 --> 00:00:46.776
- [Roger] Being big fans,
we went to the matinee show

00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:49.238
and watched the Mothers
of Invention and Frank.

00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:51.536
About an hour or so into the show,

00:00:51.536 --> 00:00:54.900
someone had fired a flare
gun into the ceiling.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.456
(gun shooting)

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.104
- [Narrator] The concert abruptly ended

00:00:58.104 --> 00:01:00.427
and once everyone exited safely,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:03.910
- [Roger] Within five
minutes, flames everywhere.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.602
And it raged, it was just
a massive fire and went on,

00:01:07.602 --> 00:01:10.225
in fact it went on through the night.

00:01:10.225 --> 00:01:13.360
- [Narrator] The concert
hall was reduced to ashes.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.612
Deep Purple eventually found new space

00:01:15.612 --> 00:01:18.979
and feverishly recorded
their sixth studio album.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:20.465
There was one problem, though.

00:01:20.465 --> 00:01:22.834
- [Roger] We realized
we were a song short.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.273
- [Narrator] So the band improvised.

00:01:24.273 --> 00:01:25.481
And had an idea.

00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:27.478
- [Roger] Why don't we write
a song about what happened

00:01:27.478 --> 00:01:28.964
to us here in Montreux.

00:01:28.964 --> 00:01:31.030
The whole adventure of
trying to make a record

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.422
and the place burning down.

00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:35.419
- [Narrator] Just then,
Roger remembered a vision

00:01:35.419 --> 00:01:37.137
he had back in Montreux.

00:01:37.137 --> 00:01:40.597
- [Roger] About a day
or two after the fire,

00:01:40.597 --> 00:01:43.680
I woke up one morning with four words

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.913
that I'd apparently said out loud.

00:01:46.913 --> 00:01:48.445
They seemed to be hanging in the room

00:01:48.445 --> 00:01:49.278
as I opened my eyes.

00:01:49.278 --> 00:01:50.350
(whispering)

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.020
And I kinda said to myself,
what did I just say?

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.921
Smoke on the water or something like that.

00:01:56.921 --> 00:01:57.966
Smoke on the water.

00:01:57.966 --> 00:01:59.893
Well that could be the story of the fire.

00:01:59.893 --> 00:02:03.642
And so we sat down and
literally wrote the words to it

00:02:03.642 --> 00:02:05.570
in probably about 15 minutes.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.656
♫ We all came out to Montreux

00:02:09.656 --> 00:02:13.573
♫ On the Lake Geneva shoreline

00:02:15.206 --> 00:02:17.760
♫ But some stupid with a flare gun

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.684
♫ Burned the place to the ground

00:02:21.684 --> 00:02:25.469
Smoke on the water, fire in the sky.

00:02:25.469 --> 00:02:27.907
- [Narrator] The song became
a surprise hit for the band,

00:02:27.907 --> 00:02:30.438
but also taught Roger a valuable lesson.

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:31.947
- [Roger] You’re at your best when you're

00:02:31.947 --> 00:02:33.434
not trying too hard.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.547
I think you have more
fun when you don't know

00:02:35.547 --> 00:02:37.149
that anything's gonna come of it.

00:02:37.149 --> 00:02:39.566
(rock music)

